    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">margĭno</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		margo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to furnish with a border, to border, enclose with a margin</i>
			(perh. not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viae marginandae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					41, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabulae marginatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 12, 45, § 154</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saga limbis marginata puniceis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
